{"kind":"artifact","text":"The remote a repository advertises is read from its own local configuration only, bounded, and admitted only when safe to link. Exact clean pushed head 7da8b753682d38aa118e709943df0ee8c03e5c37 on request/repo-remote-link; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 29ac34a8, checkout clean, main untouched at 02558e8d. Under planner's child 48ec44db and my promise ca8d07ed.\n\nPROVENANCE, WHICH IS THE ONLY THING THAT CHANGED SINCE 512f5c5f. The tree is byte-identical at 29ac34a8; the commit was amended so its Rests-On names planner's repair child 48ec44db rather than the parent dd883da0. Codex refused the previous delivery at e0b657b8 and was right: a ratified changes-requested verdict authorizes nothing, and a head whose trailer does not reach the row authorizing it cannot carry a review. The seven artifacts at the old head are retired.\n\nTHE DEFECT CODEX FOUND. gitRemotes ran git config without --local, so command-scope and global configuration contributed remote.origin.url. I reproduced it before changing anything: an injected GIT_CONFIG_COUNT origin is emitted second, and gitRemotes keys a map by remote name, so the injected URL wins. I had built an allowlist for the URL's scheme and never asked whether the URL was the repository's to begin with — a scheme check on an attacker-supplied address is no protection at all.\n\nTHE FIX. config --local --null --get-regexp, with three regressions following an injected outer-scope origin through gitRemotes, LocalRepo and the live /v0/worktrees body. Bounds at 64 KiB of output and 64 remotes, both failing closed rather than truncating, because a truncated set would make which remote gets linked depend on where reading stopped.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Removing --local fails TestGitRemotesReadsRepositoryLocalConfigurationOnly and TestLocalWorktreesIgnoresOutOfRepositoryRemoteConfiguration, both reporting the attacker URL where the repository's own origin belongs. Restored; internal/app/app.go sha256 1088a87d577f49a737b3aa8aa322ef9f584d386ea55b8e8f873edcb7cd248e21 before and after.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from a clean run I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 35 packages, zero failures and zero cached, cmd/gs 280.551s and internal/docset 104.127s; npm test --prefix ui 98/98; gofmt -l . empty; go build and go vet exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"7da8b753682d38aa118e709943df0ee8c03e5c37","path":"internal/app"}}